        "\n",
        "I was writing my masters thesis about the connection between a\n",
        "generalization of the reidemeister-torsion (called $\\ell^2$-alexander torsion)\n",
        "and the [thurston norm](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thurston_norm) of\n",
        "3-manifolds.\n",
        "Check it out, if you like:\n",
        "\n",
        "<iframe\n",
        "  src=\"/masterarbeit\"\n",
        "  style=\"width:100%; height:600px; border:none;\"\n",
        "  title=\"Masterarbeit PDF\"\n",
        "  height=\"600\"\n",
        "></iframe>\n",
        "\n",
        "[Masterarbeit.pdf](/masterarbeit)\n",
        "\n",
        "Some pictures of it can be found [here](https://www.instagram.com/stories/highlights/18097883624515441/).\n",
        "\n",
        "## How To Read This Thesis\n",
        "\n",
        "I have used hyperlinks extensively. Especially the main part (section 4) is very\n",
        "short, as it links to previous results and definitions.\n",
        "Here is an example of how to read the thesis:\n",
        "(In dark mode the hyperlinks are highlighted in a light blue color, so they are\n",
        "easier to spot. In light mode they also work, but they are not highlighted, as\n",
        "my supervisor wanted)\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {layout-ncol=3}\n",
        "![Let us look at lemma 4.24 which proofs the main theorem for manifolds whose\n",
        "JSJ-decomposition contains a hyperbolic part.\n",
        "In the proof, we can just click to where the JSJ-decomposition is defined.](./assets/highlighted-links.png){.lightbox group=\"how-to-read\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "![After clicking on \"JSJ-Zerlegung\", the definition is shown.\n",
        "We are also shown directly what hyperbolic parts are. \n",
        "We also have directly above a few examples (3d-renders) of how such an incompressible torus\n",
        "of the JSJ-decomposition might look like (here a seifert part).](./assets/following-links.png){.lightbox group=\"how-to-read\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "![When clicking on \"incompressible\", we also have directly the definition \n",
        "together with a visualization of it.](./assets/following-links2.png){.lightbox group=\"how-to-read\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "![The definition of \"incompressible\" however used \"proper embedding\" internally,\n",
        "which is also reachable by hyperlink and visualized.](./assets/following-links3.png){.lightbox group=\"how-to-read\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "![Next up in the proof, \"hyperbolic\" is used. \n",
        "We can follow this definition twice, until it is completely unfolded.](./assets/following-links4.png){.lightbox group=\"how-to-read\"}\n",
        "\n",
