        "We can follow this (1) to its definition, where these are defined as limits of \"fibered classes\",\n",
        "which we can again look up (2). I have defined them in a non-standard way \n",
        "(equivalent to the standard definition, but I found my way more intuitive) and \n",
        "I provided examples for them (3) and counterexamples as well (4).](./assets/following-links5.png){.lightbox group=\"how-to-read\"}\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "This also explains why the main part is so short.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Critique\n",
        "\n",
        "My thesis was criticized, and the main points of critique boil down to the\n",
        "following points:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. There were too many visualizations and examples\n",
        "2. Some examples (like the \"physical interpretation\") of reidemeister torsion\n",
        "  and its applications to physics were too far reaching\n",
        "3. I used non-standard notation\n",
        "\n",
        "Here is what I learned from it:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. I have created a lot of visualizations, like this one:\n",
        "\n",
        "   ::: {layout-ncol=3}\n",
        "   ![3d renders of a car in a tube](./assets/thesis-car.png){.lightbox}\n",
        "   :::\n",
        "\n",
        "   However, I was inspired by classical textbooks like\n",
        "   \"William L. Burke, Applied Differential Geometry (Cambridge University Press, 1985).\",\n",
        "   which had similarily many visualization (also similar in content):\n",
        "   and also the classic [Conway's classical ZIP proof](https://webhomes.maths.ed.ac.uk/~v1ranick/papers/francisweeks.pdf) of the classification of surfaces,\n",
        "   which uses pants and zippers to visualize the core ideas from geometry and topology:\n",
        "\n",
        "   ::: {layout-ncol=3}\n",
        "   ![William L. Burke, Applied Differential Geometry (Cambridge University Press, 1985), pp 44](../../assets/assets/burke-car.png){.lightbox group=\"various-visualizations\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "   ![Conways zip proof](../../assets/assets/conway-zip.png){.lightbox group=\"various-visualizations\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "   ![George K. Francis, A Topological Picturebook, 2007](./assets/topological-picture-book.png){.lightbox group=\"various-visualizations\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "   ![George K. Francis, A Topological Picturebook, 2007](./assets/topologicalpicturebook2.png){.lightbox group=\"various-visualizations\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "   ![I was told my visualizations should have been more technical, like this visualization of a triangulation of a surface from \"Holger Kammeyer, Introduction to Algebraic Topology (Springer International Publishing, 2022)\"](../../assets/assets/kammeyer-simplicial.png){.lightbox group=\"various-visualizations\"}\n",
        "   :::\n",
        "\n",
        "2. Regarding the physical interpretation, and general references to\n",
        "   physics/cosmology, I might have dug too deep, which made my thesis too long and too far reaching.\n",
        "   For the next thesis I will reduce its scope to easy the life of my correctors\n",
        "   and readers.\n",
        "\n",
        "   ::: {layout-ncol=3}\n",
        "   ![A short except from the passage about physical interpretations](../../assets/assets/electro-magnetism.png)\n",
        "   :::\n",
        "   \n",
        "3. Fair enough, I used $\\lll$ and $\\ggg$ instead of $\\lambda$ and $\\rho$ for\n",
        "   the left and right regular representation. I still think regarding currying that\n",
        "   this was the right choice. It also more closely aligns with\n",
        "   how group actions are usually denoted as $a \\triangleright x$ for $a \\in G$\n",
        "   and $x \\in X$ with $G \\curvearrowright X$.\n",
        "   \n",
        "   ::: {layout-ncol=3}\n",
        "   ![Left and right actions using \"weird\"\n",
        "   notation](../../assets/assets/rrr.png){.lightbox group=\"group-action\"}\n",
        "   ![On wikipedia, group actions are also denoted using more \"triangular\" shapes](../../assets/assets/action.png){.lightbox group=\"group-action\"}\n",
        "   :::\n",
        "\n",
        "From this I have learned that I should have asked my supervisor more often for \n",
        "feedback, as such feedback would have caught these points earlier.\n",
        "\n",
